  "details": "Currently there's no way of knowing how motion sickness friendly a world is unless the world creator mentions it in the description. I propose a motion rating system that world creators would use to denote how motion sickness friendly their worlds are.\n\nI feel like at least 3 different ratings would be good enough.\n\n*Calm - Worlds that require little to no movement and don't contain gimmicks that forcibly move the player. Examples: Price Guess, Quick, Draw!, Cards Against Humanity.\n\n*Mild - Worlds that require a lot of movement but are generally not too fast paced and keep players upright most of the time. Examples: Prison Escape, Blackout, Ghost.\n\n*Extreme - World that contain very fast movement and can spin the player around a lot. Examples: Test Pilots, Go Kart Zombie Tag, Super VR Ball.\n\nSome crudely drawn example icons. Icons like these could be displayed on the world thumbnail, in the details, and on the portal.",
